From: UTDeck
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: decide fullscreen and fill by the window's client area

Patches 0006 and 0010 decide how a game's swapchain is shown by comparing the window's rect with its
monitor: equal is a fullscreen game (scaled over the monitor, the window left as it is), smaller is
fill (the window made fullscreen over a black buffer, the picture fitted into it). A window with a
title bar exactly the monitor's size counted as fullscreen, although its picture is smaller.

Need for Speed Most Wanted (2012) on our base, at 1280x720 (an emulated mode): Lomiri put another
window in front for a moment, DXVK left fullscreen, and the game came back as a window with a title
bar, 1280x720 outside and 1280x700 inside (its swapchain recreated at 1280x700). It was taken for a
fullscreen game: the picture under a title bar Wayland does not draw (a stripe of the wallpaper on
top) and the wallpaper left and right instead of black bars (the Nothing Phone (1), stage 4.10).

Both checks now use the client area (in screen coordinates): a borderless fullscreen window is
unchanged; a window with a frame is shown by fill, as a smaller window already is.
---
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -1942,7 +1942,10 @@
     return mode;
 }
 
-/* Whether hwnd covers its whole monitor (a fullscreen game); if so, the monitor in raw coordinates. */
+/* Whether hwnd's picture (its client area) covers its whole monitor (a fullscreen game); if so, the
+ * monitor in raw coordinates. The client area, not the window: a window with a title bar exactly the
+ * monitor's size (a game dropped out of fullscreen at an emulated mode, Need for Speed Most Wanted
+ * 2012 at 1280x720: its picture 1280x700) is not fullscreen, and is shown by fill instead. */
 static BOOL window_covers_monitor( HWND hwnd, RECT *raw_monitor )
 {
     UINT ctx = set_thread_dpi_awareness_context( NTUSER_DPI_PER_MONITOR_AWARE );
@@ -1951,7 +1954,7 @@
     RECT window;
     BOOL ret;
 
-    ret = get_window_rect( hwnd, &window, dpi ) && EqualRect( &window, &info.rcMonitor );
+    ret = get_client_rect_rel( hwnd, COORDS_SCREEN, &window, dpi ) && EqualRect( &window, &info.rcMonitor );
     if (ret) *raw_monitor = get_monitor_physical_rect( info.rcMonitor, dpi );
     set_thread_dpi_awareness_context( ctx );
     return ret;
@@ -2006,7 +2009,8 @@
     ctx = set_thread_dpi_awareness_context( NTUSER_DPI_PER_MONITOR_AWARE );
     dpi = get_thread_dpi();
     info = monitor_info_from_window( hwnd, MONITOR_DEFAULTTONEAREST );
-    ret = get_window_rect( hwnd, &window, dpi ) && !EqualRect( &window, &info.rcMonitor ) &&
+    /* the client area, as in window_covers_monitor: a title bar does not make a window fullscreen */
+    ret = get_client_rect_rel( hwnd, COORDS_SCREEN, &window, dpi ) && !EqualRect( &window, &info.rcMonitor ) &&
           window.right - window.left <= info.rcMonitor.right - info.rcMonitor.left &&
           window.bottom - window.top <= info.rcMonitor.bottom - info.rcMonitor.top;
     if (ret) *raw_monitor = get_monitor_physical_rect( info.rcMonitor, dpi );
